th wales hasn't seen  extreme weather like this for 100 years  and much of western sydney 50 years we  do get heavy rain i lived in london for  many years and when it rains there we  get a lot of drizzle but here in sydney  when it rains it absolutely pours and  i've often said  but even central sydney the roads the  streets are not  built for heavy rain i had to make a few  detours on friday for instance because  the road the drains the gutters were  absolutely flooded  and how would you say given your  experience well prepared  were authorities and indeed the  population for all this  well i know these state emergency  services and other emergency services  say that since thursday they've received  about  7 000 emergency calls i know also other  states have also  offered and given emergency resources as  well  i would say they are as prepared as they  could be  uh regarding the people today there are  a lot of st  patrick's day weekend celebrations i  went out to celebrate at sydney harbour  and there was certainly a lot of people  out despite the weather  but probably less than usual but the  thing we are experiencing is we will get  these heavy downpours  and then we just get a little bit of  rain so we're still able to go out but i  know parts of western sydney i'm in  central sydney have had it a lot worse  and it's predicted that  uh perhaps tomorrow and in coming days  up to 4 000 people  could be evacuated and just big  picture-wise australia hasn't  uh been having a lot of luck  weather-wise it seems  last year we saw this huge bush fires  now we've got this heavy rainfall  are people talking of a pattern of  extreme weather developing  they certainly are i mean a lot of  people previously their fears about  australia were snakes and spiders these  days  it's the weather and often states such  as queensland they get extremely hot  weather they get bush fires  new south wales has a history of  business fires but lately we've had it  pretty  difficult i mean